{"number": 22, "text": "                                                                                    SectionA  Letters and souncs\n\n\n          Exercises\n\n   5.1    Listen to the letters of the alphabet. If the letter has the sound write ee under it. If it\n    A26   has the sound /e/, write e under it. If the letter does not have or /e/, don't write anything.\n\n\n     .2   Change  the vowel sound  from /e/ to /i:/ in these words. Write the new words.\n          EXAMPLE     Met         Meat\n\n\n    6.3    Find a way from Start to Finish. You may pass a square only if the word in it has the sound /i:/.\n          You  can move  horizontally (<>) or vertically  only.\n\n\n    6.4          and  circle the word you hear. If you find any of these difficult, go to Section D4 Sound pairs\n           for further practice.\n           1 Men   or man?    Did you  see the men / man?                                              pair 1)\n           2 Pen  or pain?   I’ve got a pen/ pain in my hand.                                          pair 4)\n           3 Bear  or beer?  That’s a strong bear / beer.                                              pair 8)\n           4 Live or leave?   I want to live / leave.                                                 pair 10)\n           5 Bed  or bird?  Did  you  see the bed / bird?                                   (sound    pair 12)\n           6 Left or lift? You  should  take the left / lift.                               (=sound   pair 13)\n             Follow up: Record yourself saying the sentences in 6.4, choosing one of\n             the two words. Make a note of which words you say. Then listen to your\n             recording in about two weeks. Is it clear which words you said?\n\n\n                                                                          English Pronunciation in Use      21", "char_count": 1820, "mean_conf": 89.41, "word_count": 252, "words": [{"text": "SectionA", "x0": 1589, "y0": 21, "x1": 1756,